Flex-Basis is a CSS flexbox property which is used to explicitly set the initial size of an item. The size of an item can be set in the form of absolute lengths like 
200px or 12rem or we can use the percentage to set the length and the item will take that much space of the container.

It controls the width of an item when the flex-direction is set to 'row' and height when the flex-drection is set to 'column'.
